Understanding var and dynamic in C#-
-------------------------------------

Both var and dynamic allow flexible variable declarations, but they behave differently.


What Is var?
var is a compile-time keyword — C# automatically understands the type at compile time based on the assigned value.

Example:-
-------
 
var name = "Venkatesh";     // string
var age = 25;               // int
var price = 99.99;          // double


Key Points:
You must initialize var at the time of declaration.

The data type is fixed after compile time.

You can’t change its type later.


Example Program:-
----------------


using System;

class VarExample
{
    static void Main()
    {
        var message = "Hello"; // treated as string
        Console.WriteLine(message.ToUpper()); // Allowed

        // message = 100; ❌ Error: Can't change string to int
    }
}


-----------------------------------------------------------------------


What Is dynamic?
----------------

dynamic is a runtime type — it allows type to change while running the program.

Example:-
--------
dynamic x = "Venkatesh";   // string
x = 25;                    // now it's int
x = true;                  // now it's bool


Example Program:-
---------------

using System;

class DynamicExample
{
    static void Main()
    {
        dynamic data = "Hello";
        Console.WriteLine(data.ToUpper());

        data = 123; // Now it's int
        Console.WriteLine(data + 1); // Outputs: 124

        data = true; // Now it's bool
        Console.WriteLine("Boolean? " + data);
    }
}


Key Differences: var vs dynamic-
-------------------------------

| Feature              | `var`            | `dynamic`                       |
| -------------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------- |
| Type decided at      | Compile time ✅ | Runtime ✅                       |
| Needs initialization |  Yes            |  Not compulsory                  |
| Type can change      |  No             |  Yes                             |
| IntelliSense support |  Full           | Less                             |
| Use case             | Normal variables| External APIs, JSON, reflection  |


 Summary for Notes-
 -----------------
 
| Keyword   | Behavior     | Use When…                                 |
| --------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| `var`     | Compile-time | You know the type                         |
| `dynamic` | Runtime      | You don’t know type (e.g., JSON API data) |

